{
    "background_story": "Fernanda was a brilliant and ambitious journalist, known for her fearless investigations into the paranormal. While researching a story on Jewish mysticism, she stumbled upon an ancient text that spoke of the dybbuk, a malevolent spirit from Jewish mythology. Intrigued, Fernanda delved deeper into the legend, spending countless hours poring over dusty tomes and seeking out experts in the field. But as she dug deeper, she began to experience strange and terrifying occurrences - doors slamming shut, disembodied whispers, and an unshakeable feeling of being watched. It became clear that Fernanda had unknowingly unleashed a dybbuk, which had attached itself to her. Desperate to free herself from the entity's grasp, Fernanda turned to a local rabbi, who performed a ritual to exorcise the dybbuk. But the experience left her shaken, and Fernanda never looked at the spirit world in the same way again.",
